    "body": {
      "en": "### Week 1: Toy Recognition\n\nChildren become familiar with common toys as real objects. The focus is looking, touching, holding, showing, giving, and moving toward named toys.\n\n### Week 2: Box, Bag, In and Out\n\nChildren experience containers through opening, closing, putting toys in, and taking toys out. The focus is physical action response, not verbal explanation.\n\n### Week 3: Give, Take and Wait\n\nChildren use toy routines for adult-supported exchange and early turn-taking. The focus is taking a toy, giving a toy, waiting briefly, and joining a simple shared play sequence.\n\n### Week 4: Integrated Toy Clean-Up Routine\n\nChildren combine toy recognition, container handling, give/take routines, and clean-up into one complete classroom play sequence.",
      "zh": "### Week 1: Toy Recognition｜第一周：玩具识别\n\n儿童把常见玩具作为真实物品来熟悉。重点是看、触摸、拿、展示、给予和移向被命名的玩具。\n\n### Week 2: Box, Bag, In and Out｜第二周：盒子、包、放入和取出\n\n儿童通过打开、合上、把玩具放入和取出玩具来体验容器。重点是身体动作反应，而非口头解释。\n\n### Week 3: Give, Take and Wait｜第三周：给予、拿取和等待\n\n儿童使用玩具常规进行成人支持的交换和早期轮流。重点是拿一个玩具、给一个玩具、短暂等待，以及加入一个简单的共享游戏序列。\n\n### Week 4: Integrated Toy Clean-Up Routine｜第四周：整合的玩具收拾常规\n\n儿童把玩具识别、容器处理、给予／拿取常规和收拾组合成一个完整的课堂游戏序列。"
    },
